Article 3 (Composition)
(1) The Committee shall consist of not more than 50 members, including one Chairperson and two Vice Chairpersons, taking gender and regional representation into account.
(2) Members of the Committee shall be the following persons:
1. Persons engaged in civil society organizations, academia, etc. who have extensive knowledge and experience concerning comprehensive social reform and are commissioned by the Prime Minister;
2. Experts in comprehensive social reform recommended by representatives of political parties under the Political Parties Act and commissioned by the Prime Minister;
3. One public official belonging to the Senior Executive Service of the Office of the Prime Minister who is responsible for comprehensive social reform and is designated by the Prime Minister;
4. Other persons with extensive knowledge and experience concerning comprehensive social reform who are commissioned by the Prime Minister.
(3) The Chairperson of the Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Chairperson") and its Vice Chairpersons (hereinafter referred to as the "Vice Chairpersons") shall be elected by the Committee from among members specified in subparagraphs 1, 2 or 4 of paragraph (2) (hereinafter referred to as "commissioned members").
